   "daf": "88a",
   "sentenceId": 12,
   "he": "כָּתַב חֲנִיכָתוֹ וַחֲנִיכָתָהּ – כָּשֵׁר. תָּנוּ רַבָּנַן: חֲנִיכַת אָבוֹת בְּגִיטִּין – עַד עֲשָׂרָה דּוֹרוֹת. רַבִּי שִׁמְעוֹן בֶּן אֶלְעָזָר אוֹמֵר: שְׁלֹשָׁה דּוֹרוֹת – כָּשֵׁר, מִכָּאן וְאֵילָךְ – פָּסוּל.",
   "en": "§ It is stated in the mishna: With regard to the names of the husband and wife, if the scribe «wrote his surname» or nickname «and her surname» or nickname, it is «valid. The Sages taught» (Tosefta 8:6): «A surname» from one’s «forefathers» is valid «with regard to bills of divorce until ten generations» after the forefather. «Rabbi Shimon ben Elazar says:» It is «valid» for only «three generations; from this» point «forward» it is «invalid.»"
  }
